# Supabase – copy to `.env.local` and fill the anon key from the dashboard.
# Dashboard: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/ljwvujxgobnynomrmnyv/settings/api

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ljwvujxgobnynomrmnyv.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-from-settings-api

# Server-only: enables profile photo upload without pre-creating the Storage bucket (Settings → API → service_role).
# Never expose this key to the browser or commit it to git.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# --- Google / X (Supabase → Authentication → Providers) ---
# Site URL + Redirect URLs: include https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback,
# http://localhost:3000/auth/callback, and production …/auth/callback.
# Google / X: enable provider and paste OAuth client id + secret from each developer console.
#
# --- Telegram Login ---
# 1. @BotFather → /newbot → **TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN** (server only, never commit).
# 2. **SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY** (server only) — same as avatar uploads; required for session creation.
# 3. @BotFather → **/setdomain** → **one real website hostname** (no `https://`, no path, no `:3000`).
#    Many accounts reject **`localhost`** (“should contain one domain name”); use your **production host**
#    (e.g. `esco-bets.vercel.app`) or a **tunnel host** (ngrok / Cloudflare Tunnel) and open the app only via that URL.
# 4. Restart dev after env changes. Telegram uses `Telegram.Login.auth` (popup); `origin` must match the linked domain.
# Docs: https://core.telegram.org/widgets/login

# Optional — “Open X (support)” link after account → Change password → forgot / need help (e.g. your X profile or messages URL).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_X_URL=https://x.com/YourEscoBetsSupport

# Password reset email: configure **Supabase → Authentication → Emails** (and SMTP if you use a custom provider).
# Redirect URLs allow-list must include **/reset-password** (e.g. https://your-app.vercel.app/reset-password and http://localhost:3000/reset-password) plus /auth/callback for OAuth.
